# Non-secret parameters for the four-symbol LSE tail import.
# The API key stays only in the root-owned /etc/forexbot/lse.env.
#
# The tail is what keeps the ORCA-4 panel from being a month stale. It re-reads
# a short recent window for ALL four symbols so the materializer can prove the
# overlapping D1 bars are identical to the sealed history before appending
# anything. Choose a NEW output path for every run: the importer publishes
# atomically and refuses to replace an existing target.
LSE_OUTPUT_DIR=/var/lib/forexbot-backtest/incoming/fxgold-tail-2026-lse-v1
# Same order and same bot symbols as the ORCA-4 universe profile. GOLD must be
# mapped explicitly because London Strategic Edge catalogues it as XAU/USD.
LSE_SYMBOLS="EURUSD GBPUSD USDCAD GOLD=XAU/USD"
# Start well before the sealed FX snapshot ends (D1 close 2026-07-23T21:00Z) so
# the overlap is large enough to be evidence rather than a coincidence, and the
# first partially covered D1 bucket can be dropped without losing the overlap.
LSE_START=2026-07-01
# Exclusive. Move this forward on every re-import; the previous D1 bar must be
# fully closed, so an end of D only publishes bars closing before D.
LSE_END=2026-08-23
# Paced UTC date-window REST. The range is short but has four symbols, which
# would need four export jobs and burn the hourly export quota for no benefit.
LSE_TRANSPORT=rest
# Must stay empty: this run mixes the fx and commodity datasets, so each symbol
# is resolved and validated against the LSE catalog individually.
LSE_DATASET=
LSE_BAR_TIMEZONE=Europe/Athens
# ORCA consumes D1 only. The importer always retains its canonical M1 source as
# well, so this produces <SYMBOL>_1m.parquet and <SYMBOL>_1d.parquet.
LSE_TIMEFRAMES="1d"
LSE_REST_MIN_INTERVAL=0.35
# Identical quality gates to the sealed FX snapshot. Any relaxation here would
# change how D1 buckets are aggregated and break the exact-overlap check that
# authorises the splice.
LSE_MIN_BUCKET_COVERAGE=0.95
LSE_MAX_EDGE_GAP_DAYS=4
LSE_MAX_INTERNAL_GAP_DAYS=4
